 C's cooperation and openness: no explicit observations, but noted show-off and not open to new ideas.\n\nNow Agent 2 must make a public contribution: state current recommendation, refer to discussion, use explicit facts, explain implications.\n\nWe need to decide whether to support C or not. We have concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas, no evidence of crew cooperation. Also other candidates have some strengths: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, but makes nasty remarks about colleagues (communication issue). A can make quick correct decisions, keeps calm in crisis, understands complicated technology, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. D responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, but hot temper, know-it-all, etc.\n\nWe need to weigh. The leading candidate is C, but we have concerns about crew cooperation and feedback. We have no evidence for others on crew cooperation either, but B makes nasty remarks, which is a clear negative for crew cooperation and professional communication. A difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric also negative. D hot temper and know-it-all also negative.\n\nThus C still seems strongest overall despite concerns. We can state we still recommend C, but we need to highlight that we need to address the cooperation concerns, maybe propose training. Or we could ask for more info on other candidates' crew cooperation. But the instruction: each turn should be a focused argumentative contribution, referencing discussion, using facts, and stating vote.\n\nThus we can say: I remain inclined to recommend C, because his technical and leadership strengths are critical for long-distance flights, and the concerns about being a show\u2011off and not open to new ideas are not yet substantiated with concrete crew conflict, whereas other candidates have clear communication or temperament issues (B's nasty remarks, A's egocentric communication difficulty, D's hot temper). Therefore C remains best.\n\nWe should include explicit facts: C anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: regarded as show\u2011off, not open to new ideas. For others: B makes nasty remarks, A difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, D hot temper, know-it-all.\n\nThus vote for C.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
