lic contribution: state current recommendation, refer to discussion, use explicit facts, explain.\n\nWe need to consider if we want to keep recommending C or change. Based on evidence, C still strongest technical, but concerns about show-off and not open to new ideas, and lack of crew cooperation evidence. Others have more concrete negative issues: B's nasty remarks, A's communication difficulty, D's hot temper and unknown crew cooperation. So likely still recommend C, with note about need for onboarding.\n\nThus we will produce a public message: agree with Agent 1, reaffirm recommendation for C, referencing the facts: C anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, leadership; concerns: show-off, not open to new ideas; other candidates have more concrete issues: B's grumpy/uncooperative, A's egocentric and communication difficulty, D's hot temper and know-it-all, plus lack of evidence on stress resilience. So we keep vote for C.\n\nWe must include explicit facts: from notes. Provide reasoning.\n\nNow produce METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
